.TH VOP_RMDIR 9 "February 6, 2026" "Substrate" "Kernel Developer's Manual"
.SH NAME
VOP_RMDIR \- remove a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <vfs/vnode.h>
.B #include <sys/namei.h>
.PP
.BI "int VOP_RMDIR(struct vnode *dvp, struct vnode *vp, struct componentname *cnp);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B VOP_RMDIR()
function removes an empty directory.
.PP
The arguments are:
.TP
.I dvp
The vnode of the parent directory.
.TP
.I vp
The vnode of the directory to be removed.
.TP
.I cnp
The component name information for the directory to be removed.
.SH LOCKS
The parent directory
.I dvp
and the directory
.I vp
should be locked on entry and will remain locked on return.
.SH RETURN VALUES
Zero is returned on success, otherwise an error code is returned.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
[ENOTDIR]
The
.I dvp
argument is not a directory, or
.I vp
is not a directory.
.TP
[ENOTEMPTY]
The directory
.I vp
is not empty.
.TP
[EBUSY]
The directory
.I vp
is in use (e.g., a mount point).
.TP
[EACCES]
Permission denied.
.TP
[EROFS]
The filesystem is read-only.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vnode (9),
.BR VOP_REMOVE (9)
